  "title": "Subject-Verb Agreement",
  "subject": "Language Arts",
  "term": 2,
  "icon": "🤝",
  "description": "The subject and verb must be best friends and match!",
  "video": {
    "youtubeId": "ZqtqnNFfDXE",
    "title": "Verbs Part 2: Subject-Verb Agreement",
    "channel": "Mind Blooming"
  },
  "steps": [
    "The subject (who) and the verb (action) must MATCH.",
    "ONE person or thing → verb gets -s: 'The dog runs.' 'She sings.'",
    "MORE than one → no -s: 'The dogs run.' 'They sing.'",
    "Use IS and HAS for one; ARE and HAVE for more than one: 'He is...', 'They are...'"
  ],
  "check": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "id": "check",
        "title": "Did you get it?",
        "description": "Let's see what you remember!",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "q1",
            "type": "multiple-choice",
            "prompt": "Which fits? 'The bird ___ in the tree.'",
            "correct": "sings",
            "hint": "One bird → verb gets -s.",
            "options": [
              "sings",
              "sing",
              "singing",
              "are sing"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "q2",
            "type": "multiple-choice",
            "prompt": "Which fits? 'The children ___ cricket.'",
            "correct": "play",
            "hint": "More than one → no -s.",
            "options": [
              "play",
              "plays",
              "is playing",
              "playses"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "q3",
            "type": "multiple-choice",
            "prompt": "Which fits? 'She ___ a new book.'",
